 "description": "A fast-growing, short-lived pine of the foggy central coast, conical when young and later round or flat-topped and irregular. Its bright green needles come in threes, and lopsided cones stay closed on the branches for years until fire or heat opens them.",
 "season_notes": {
  "winter": "Rain-soaked and bright green; closed cones cling in whorls along the limbs.",
  "spring": "Pale new candles stand at the branch tips and yellow pollen drifts in March.",
  "summer": "Fog drips from the long needles, watering the ground beneath.",
  "fall": "A few old cones split open in warm dry days and drop winged seeds."
